1
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:15,000
Of all the lives he changed, the one that changed the most was his own.

2
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:24,000
Mr. Holland's Opus is a drama, music film directed by Stephen Herek.

3
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:33,000
In 1965, passionate musician Glenn Holland takes a day job as a high school music teacher, convinced
it's just a small obstacle on the road to his true calling: writing a historic opus.

4
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:42,000
As the decades roll by with the composition unwritten but generations of students
inspired through his teaching, Holland must redefine his life's purpose.

5
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Glenn Holland, played by Richard Dreyfuss.

6
00:42:54,000 --> 00:43:00,000
Iris Holland, played by Glenne Headly.

7
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:09,000
Bill Meister, played by Jay Thomas.

8
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
Principal Jacobs, played by Olympia Dukakis.

9
01:04:21,000 --> 01:04:27,000
Vice Principal Gene Wolters, played by William H. Macy.

10
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Gertrude Lang, played by Alicia Witt.

11
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:45,000
Holland's Opus is a 1995 American drama film directed by
Stephen Herek, produced by Ted Field, Robert W.

12
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:54,000
Cort, and Michael Nolin, and written by Patrick Sheane Duncan.

13
01:32:57,000 --> 01:33:03,000
The film stars Richard Dreyfuss in the title role of Glenn Holland, a dedicated high school music teacher who attempts to
compose his own music while struggling to balance his job and life with his wife and profoundly deaf son.

14
01:40:06,000 --> 01:40:12,000
The cast also includes Glenne Headly, Olympia Dukakis, William H.

15
01:47:15,000 --> 01:47:21,000
Macy, and Jay Thomas.

16
01:54:24,000 --> 01:54:30,000
The film was nominated for the Golden Globe Award for Best Screenplay in 1995.

17
02:01:33,000 --> 02:01:39,000
Richard Dreyfuss received nominations for the Golden Globe Award for Best Actor
– Motion Picture Drama and the Academy Award for Best Actor.

18
02:08:42,000 --> 02:08:48,000
The film explores themes of high school, husband wife
relationship, composer, music teacher, mentor.

19
02:15:51,000 --> 02:15:57,000
The tone is uplifting and emotional.
